IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-23.l4 -- ARTICLE 23 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RESTRICTIONS (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 282-303 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the Section 5 heading at
-- 280-281 and the two heading lines of Article 23 at 282-283 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--
-- WHOSE.  Article 23 is addressed to a lawmaker: Union or Member State law MAY restrict the scope of the obligations and
-- rights of Articles 12 to 22 and 34 (and Article 5 in part).  In the Hohfeld table it is a POWER of the lawmaker, and the
-- LIABILITY of controllers and data subjects (their rights and duties can be cut back by it).  No seat is a lawmaker, so
-- the two seats ask what it means to them: may a law restrict this right or this duty; does the law restricting it contain
-- what paragraph 2 requires.  No regulative rule is written (the party is a law, not a role of the Regulation).
-- NOT WIRED IN.  The rights and duties of Articles 12 to 22 are encoded as the Regulation states them; a law restricting
-- one of them is NOT an input of those functions (it would add an input to every function).  A caller with such a law
-- asks `Art 23(1) ...` and treats the restricted right or duty as not covered (NOTES, Findings and Open questions).
-- THE LISTS.  The provisions whose scope may be restricted, the objectives of points (a) to (j) and the specific provisions of
-- paragraph 2 are constructors.  Paragraph 1 does not close its list of objectives with "only", and point (e) is open
-- ("other important objectives of general public interest"), so an objective outside the ten is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE.
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 23(1) provision whose scope is restricted` IS ONE OF
    `Art 23(1) an obligation or a right provided for in Articles 12 to 22`
    `Art 23(1) an obligation provided for in Article 34`
    `Art 23(1) Article 5, in so far as its provisions correspond to the rights and obligations provided for in Articles 12 to 22`
    `Art 23(1) some other provision of the Regulation`

DECLARE `Art 23(1) objective safeguarded` IS ONE OF
    `Art 23(1)(a) national security`
    `Art 23(1)(b) defence`
    `Art 23(1)(c) public security`
    `Art 23(1)(d) the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security`
    `Art 23(1)(e) other important objectives of general public interest of the Union or of a Member State, in particular an important economic or financial interest, including monetary, budgetary and taxation matters, public health and social security`
    `Art 23(1)(f) the protection of judicial independence and judicial proceedings`
    `Art 23(1)(g) the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of breaches of ethics for regulated professions`
    `Art 23(1)(h) a monitoring, inspection or regulatory function connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g)`
    `Art 23(1)(i) the protection of the data subject or the rights and freedoms of others`
    `Art 23(1)(j) the enforcement of civil law claims`
    `Art 23(1) some other objective`

DECLARE `Art 23(2) specific provision` IS ONE OF
    `Art 23(2)(a) the purposes of the processing or categories of processing`
    `Art 23(2)(b) the categories of personal data`
    `Art 23(2)(c) the scope of the restrictions introduced`
    `Art 23(2)(d) the safeguards to prevent abuse or unlawful access or transfer`
    `Art 23(2)(e) the specification of the controller or categories of controllers`
    `Art 23(2)(f) the storage periods and the applicable safeguards taking into account the nature, scope and purposes of the processing or categories of processing`
    `Art 23(2)(g) the risks to the rights and freedoms of data subjects`
    `Art 23(2)(h) the right of data subjects to be informed about the restriction`

§ `Article 23(1): what Union or Member State law may restrict`

-- src:284 | 1. Union or Member State law to which the data controller or processor is subject may restrict by way of a legislative measure the scope of the obligations and rights provided for in Articles 12 to 22 and Article 34, as well as Article 5 in so far as its provisions correspond to the rights and obligations provided for in Articles 12 to 22, when such a restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms and is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard:
-- src:285 | (a) national security;
-- src:286 | (b) defence;
-- src:287 | (c) public security;
-- src:288 | (d) the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security;
-- src:289 | (e) other important objectives of general public interest of the Union or of a Member State, in particular an important economic or financial interest of the Union or of a Member State, including monetary, budgetary and taxation a matters, public health and social security;
-- src:290 | (f) the protection of judicial independence and judicial proceedings;
-- src:291 | (g) the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of breaches of ethics for regulated professions;
-- src:292 | (h) a monitoring, inspection or regulatory function connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g);
-- src:293 | (i) the protection of the data subject or the rights and freedoms of others;
-- src:294 | (j) the enforcement of civil law claims.
@ref Art 23(1) chapeau and points (a) to (j) (src:284-294)
GIVEN `the law is Union law or Member State law to which the controller or processor is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is by way of a legislative measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision whose scope the law restricts` IS AN `Art 23(1) provision whose scope is restricted`
      `the objective the restriction safeguards` IS AN `Art 23(1) objective safeguarded`
      `the function is connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1) Union or Member State law may restrict by way of a legislative measure the scope of the obligations and rights` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the law is Union law or Member State law to which the controller or processor is subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Union or Member State law to which the data controller or processor is subject": another source of restriction is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it
        IF NOT (`the restriction is by way of a legislative measure`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by way of a legislative measure": a restriction by another means is outside the grant
        IF `the provision whose scope the law restricts` EQUALS `Art 23(1) some other provision of the Regulation`
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the scope of the obligations and rights provided for in Articles 12 to 22 and Article 34, as well as Article 5 in so far as its provisions correspond to the rights and obligations provided for in Articles 12 to 22": a restriction of another provision is outside the grant
        IF `the objective the restriction safeguards` EQUALS `Art 23(1) some other objective`
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the objectives are listed in points (a) to (j) without "only" and point (e) is open ("other important objectives of general public interest"); an objective outside them is not decided by the text
        IF `the objective the restriction safeguards` EQUALS `Art 23(1)(h) a monitoring, inspection or regulatory function connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g)` AND NOT (`the function is connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) a monitoring, inspection or regulatory function connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g)": a function with no such connection is not point (h)
        IF `the restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms` AND `the restriction is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "when", periods ruling (b) with the delegated ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; a grant named "may restrict", split site (ii), fork F23-1; the other reading is NOTHING): "when such a restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms and is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard"

-- src:284 | 1. Union or Member State law to which the data controller or processor is subject may restrict by way of a legislative measure the scope of the obligations and rights provided for in Articles 12 to 22 and Article 34, as well as Article 5 in so far as its provisions correspond to the rights and obligations provided for in Articles 12 to 22, when such a restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms and is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard:
-- src:285 | (a) national security;
-- src:286 | (b) defence;
-- src:287 | (c) public security;
-- src:288 | (d) the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security;
-- src:289 | (e) other important objectives of general public interest of the Union or of a Member State, in particular an important economic or financial interest of the Union or of a Member State, including monetary, budgetary and taxation a matters, public health and social security;
-- src:290 | (f) the protection of judicial independence and judicial proceedings;
-- src:291 | (g) the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of breaches of ethics for regulated professions;
-- src:292 | (h) a monitoring, inspection or regulatory function connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in the cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g);
-- src:293 | (i) the protection of the data subject or the rights and freedoms of others;
-- src:294 | (j) the enforcement of civil law claims.
@ref Art 23(1) the law is a necessary and proportionate measure to safeguard the objectives (the answer Article 6(4) asks for) (src:284-294)
GIVEN `the objective the restriction safeguards` IS AN `Art 23(1) objective safeguarded`
      `the law constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1) the law is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard one of the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the objective the restriction safeguards` EQUALS `Art 23(1) some other objective`
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an objective outside points (a) to (j) is not decided by the text
        IF `the law constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "when", periods ruling (b); fork F23-1): "when such a restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms and is a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard"

§ `Article 23(2): what the legislative measure must contain`

-- src:295 | 2. In particular, any legislative measure referred to in paragraph 1 shall contain specific provisions at least, where relevant, as to:
-- src:296 | (a) the purposes of the processing or categories of processing;
-- src:297 | (b) the categories of personal data;
-- src:298 | (c) the scope of the restrictions introduced;
-- src:299 | (d) the safeguards to prevent abuse or unlawful access or transfer;
-- src:300 | (e) the specification of the controller or categories of controllers;
-- src:301 | (f) the storage periods and the applicable safeguards taking into account the nature, scope and purposes of the processing or categories of processing;
-- src:302 | (g) the risks to the rights and freedoms of data subjects; and
-- src:303 | (h) the right of data subjects to be informed about the restriction, unless that may be prejudicial to the purpose of the restriction.
@ref Art 23(2) chapeau and points (a) to (h) (src:295-303)
GIVEN `the specific provisions that are relevant to the restriction` IS A LIST OF `Art 23(2) specific provision`
      `the specific provisions that the legislative measure contains` IS A LIST OF `Art 23(2) specific provision`
      `informing the data subjects about the restriction may be prejudicial to the purpose of the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(2) the legislative measure contains specific provisions at least, where relevant, as to the matters that paragraph 2 lists` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN x YIELD elem x `the specific provisions that the legislative measure contains`
                                OR (x EQUALS `Art 23(2)(h) the right of data subjects to be informed about the restriction` AND `informing the data subjects about the restriction may be prejudicial to the purpose of the restriction`))
          `the specific provisions that are relevant to the restriction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "any legislative measure referred to in paragraph 1 shall contain specific provisions at least, where relevant, as to"
    -- (h) "unless that may be prejudicial to the purpose of the restriction": a provision on informing the data subjects is not required when informing may prejudice the purpose.
    -- "where relevant": each item is required only where the caller lists it as relevant; "In particular" and "at least": the list is a minimum, so provisions on other matters do no harm and are not read.
